iet  to a keto diet this transition might not  be smooth  your body might undergo some flu-like  symptoms which includes nausea vomiting  constipation diarrhea headache and many  things more and this kind of keto flu is  kind of normal because body is  undergoing a metabolic transition  body learns how to use fat as a primary  energy source instead of glucose so in  this transition state this kind of  disbalance and this kind of symptoms  does appear and it's nothing to worry  about  keto diet has multiple health benefits  starting from weight loss  increased energy and good cardiovascular  wealth  and then it has  been proven to be important for  increasing cognitive ability  lastly in order to control blood glucose  level keto diet is really important but  there are several myths associated with  keto diet like keto right is really  dangerous if you have diabetes  now it's not really true  because the ketogenic diet has actually  been  validated by american diabetic  association and it's it turns out to be  really useful for controlling blood  sugar in type 2 diabetes patient  there are  other myths like keto diet is bad for  heart because it has a lot of fat so it  might cause problem in your  cardiovascular health but it's not true  because if you have  a lot of  fat in your  circulation  it is bad because it might get deposited  on the arteries but under ketogenic  state body knows how to utilize it  so nothing would be actually deposited  on the arteries right  now in the keto diet when we consume  more fat if we can  make sure that our fat comes from very  healthy sources like salmon like olive  oils that which are enriched in  omega-3 fatty acids then it would be  really really beneficial for your  cardiovascular health  so overall ketogenesis  and ketogenic diet could be proven  useful  to improve your cardiac health and it is  known to increase good cholesterol or  hdl level  now i hope that was useful if you like  this video give it a quick thumbs up  don